    "md5": "1040272f6ef128013e3eff8620fe0e66",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1973,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka-Russia Business Council Members\u2019 Night 2026\n\nDr. Saman Weerasinghe delivering his address, reflecting on his distinguished diplomatic career and contributions to strengthening Sri Lanka-Russia relations\n\nRussian Ambassador Levan S. Dzhagaryan delivering his address, emphasising the strengthening of Sri Lanka-Russia diplomatic and economic relations\n\nThe Sri Lanka-Russia Business Council (SLRBC) of The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce recently hosted its Members\u2019 Night, bringing together distinguished dignitaries, business leaders, and stakeholders to celebrate and further strengthen the longstanding relationship between Sri Lanka and the Russian Federation.\n\nThe event was graced by Russian Ambassador Levan S. Dzhagaryan as Chief Guest. In his address, the Ambassador reaffirmed the strong and enduring ties between the two nations and emphasised the importance of continued cooperation amidst evolving global challenges. He also noted ongoing discussions on potential collaboration in key sectors such as energy, while underscoring the importance of maintaining steady and constructive bilateral engagement.\n\nDelivering the welcome address, SLRBC President Chamath Hettiarachchi highlighted the deep-rooted friendship between Sri Lanka and Russia, built on mutual respect and cooperation. He emphasised the vast potential for expanding partnerships in areas including trade, tourism, agriculture, energy, logistics, education, and technology, noting that platforms such as the Members\u2019 Night play a vital role in fostering business connections and strengthening economic ties.\n\nA highlight of the evening was the felicitation of former Sri Lankan Ambassador to Russia Dr. Saman Weerasinghe in recognition of his contribution to enhancing bilateral relations. In his address, Dr. Weerasinghe reflected on his longstanding association with Russia and expressed gratitude for the support extended by the Russian Government and people throughout his career."
  },
