    "md5": "3afdc19fd9bdb0cdf20d87dff0a58788",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1318,
    "chunk_text": "Tomato Face Packs \u2026\n\nMix a mashed tomato with a squeeze of lemon juice and a teaspoon of honey and apply on face (avoiding eyes). Leave for 15 minutes and then rinse with cool water. (For dry skin, substitute honey with plain yoghurt.)\n\nMix a mashed tomato with a teaspoon of baking soda (avoiding sensitive areas), and apply and leave for 10 minutes, and then rinse thoroughly.\n\nMix a mashed tomato with a teaspoon of gram flour, and a touch of honey, and apply this pack and leave for 15 minutes, and then rinse with lukewarm water.\n\nMix a mashed tomato with a few drops of almond oil, and apply gently under the eyes, and leave for 15 minutes, and then rinse with cool water.\n\nMash a ripe tomato and mix with a tablespoon of plain yoghurt, and apply, and leave for 15 minutes, and then rinse with cool water.\n\nMash a ripe tomato and mix with a tablespoon of olive oil or avocado oil, and apply and let it remain for 15 minutes, and then rinse with cool water.\n\nMash a ripe tomato and mix with a teaspoon of honey and a few drops of lemon juice, and apply and let it remain for 15 minutes, and then rinse with cool water.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
