    "chunk_text": "Dockyard announces key leadership changes with strategic Board appointments\n\nCapt. (Retd.) Jagmohan appointed Chairman; Vish Govindasamy and Senthilverl Jr. join Board\n\nColombo Dockyard PLC yesterday announced significant changes to its Board of Directors, effective from 7 April 2026, marking a new chapter of strategic growth and governance excellence.\n\nFollowing its recent acquisition, India\u2019s Mazagon Dock Shipbuilders Ltd., (MDL), which now holds a 51% majority stake in Colombo Dockyard, has nominated Thimira S. Godakumbura as one of their Nominee Directors. He will continue to serve as the Managing Director and CEO of Colombo Dockyard PLC.\n\nCapt. (Retd.) Jagmohan has been appointed as the Chairman (Non-Executive) of Colombo Dockyard PLC. This landmark appointment brings a wealth of business acumen, extensive leadership experience, and visionary governance to the Board.\n\nCapt. (Retd.) Jagmohan currently serves as Chairman and Managing Director of MDL. A Naval Architect from Cochin University of Science and Technology, he holds postgraduate and M.Tech qualifications in Naval Construction and Ocean Engineering from IIT Delhi and IIT Kharagpur. With over 25 years of distinguished service in the Indian Navy, he has held key assignments in the Directorate of Naval Design and Naval Dockyard, Mumbai. His prior roles include Director at Goa Shipyard Ltd., and Chief General Manager \u2013 Design at Garden Reach Shipbuilders and Engineers Ltd., (GRSE), where he oversaw complex warship projects for the Indian Navy and Coast Guard. His appointment underscores MDL\u2019s strategic commitment to infuse Colombo Dockyard PLC\u2019s Board with unparalleled expertise, strengthening governance, operational excellence, and sustained growth.\n\nVish Govindasamy has been nominated by MDL as their Nominee Director (Non-Executive/Non-Independent)."
  },
